  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXCheckBox",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "Enable flow compensation for small infill areas.\nparameter name\t: small_area_infill_flow_compensation",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "",
    "role_desc": "toggle button",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 605.0,
    "y": 2164.0,
    "w": 20.0,
    "h": 20.0,
    "key": "small_area_infill_flow_compensation",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXTextField",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "Decrease this value slightly (for example 0.9) to reduce the amount of material for bridge, to improve sag.\n\nThe actual bridge flow used is calculated by multiplying this value with the filament flow ratio, and if set, the object's flow ratio.\nparameter name\t: bridge_flow",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "0.8",
    "role_desc": "text field",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 612.0,
    "y": 2236.0,
    "w": 103.0,
    "h": 19.0,
    "key": "bridge_flow",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXTextField",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "This value governs the thickness of the internal bridge layer. This is the first layer over sparse infill. Decrease this value slightly (for example 0.9) to improve surface quality over sparse infill.\n\nThe actual internal bridge flow used is calculated by multiplying this value with the bridge flow ratio, the filament flow ratio, and if set, the object's flow ratio.\nparameter name\t: internal_bridge_flow",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "1",
    "role_desc": "text field",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 612.0,
    "y": 2264.0,
    "w": 103.0,
    "h": 19.0,
    "key": "internal_bridge_flow",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXTextField",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "Controls the density (spacing) of external bridge lines. Default is 100%.\n\nLower density external bridges can help improve reliability as there is more space for air to circulate around the extruded bridge, improving its cooling speed. Minimum is 10%.\n\nHigher densities can produce smoother bridge surfaces, as overlapping lines provide additional support during printing. Maximum is 120%. \nNote: Bridge density that is too high can cause warping or overextrusion.\nparameter name\t: bridge_density",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "60",
    "role_desc": "text field",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 612.0,
    "y": 2292.0,
    "w": 94.0,
    "h": 19.0,
    "key": "bridge_density",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXTextField",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "Controls the density (spacing) of internal bridge lines. 100% means solid bridge. Default is 100%.\n\nLower density internal bridges can help reduce top surface pillowing and improve internal bridge reliability as there is more space for air to circulate around the extruded bridge, improving its cooling speed.\n\nThis option works particularly well when combined with the second internal bridge over infill option, further improving internal bridging structure before solid infill is extruded.\nparameter name\t: internal_bridge_density",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "100",
    "role_desc": "text field",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 612.0,
    "y": 2320.0,
    "w": 94.0,
    "h": 19.0,
    "key": "internal_bridge_density",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
  {
   "mode": "flat",
   "row": {
    "role": "AXCheckBox",
    "title": "",
    "desc": "",
    "help": "If enabled, bridges are more reliable and can bridge longer distances but may look worse. If disabled, bridges look better but are reliable only for shorter distances.\nparameter name\t: thick_bridges",
    "ident": "",
    "placeholder": "",
    "value": "",
    "role_desc": "toggle button",
    "value_num": null,
    "enabled": true,
    "x": 605.0,
    "y": 2348.0,
    "w": 20.0,
    "h": 20.0,
    "key": "thick_bridges",
    "states": [
     "flat_advanced",
     "flat_return"
    ]
   }
  },
